assistant: Subject: convert cent prices from vendor API 2026-10-01
Starting with API version 2026-10-01, the vendor returns `price` in cents (119900) instead of dollars (1199), and its published spec doesn't mention the change. `search_products` passed the value through unchanged, so agents got prices 100 times too high. The handler now reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides `price` by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Older responses are left as they are, so the v1 fixtures produce the same output. The fix doesn't change the HTTP requests sent. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. `get_product` and `get_order` also return prices and may have the same problem, but I haven't checked or changed them.

